    ☐ Create command line option balancedump @high
      ☐ Dumps in a table: (fetches from stats with --includestats *)
        ☐ Levels and Monsters:
          ☐ Level | Monster | HP | ToHitBonus | AC | XP | DMG range | Gold | Items | * # Encountered | * # PlayerFled | * # Killed | * # KillPlayer
        ☐ Player ascension:
          ☐ Level | Player Class | Level | HP Range | ToHitBonus Range | AC Range | DMG range | Avg Hits to Die | Avg Hits to Kill
            - hits to die - average monster DMG, vs. player AC, vs. Player HP = avg number of hits to kill player
              - e.g. Level 1 monsters HP average is 10, ToHitbonus is 0, DMG range is 5, and player ac at same level is 11, and HP is 12 = 12/5 = 2 hits to die at level 1
            - hits to kill - average monster HP vs Player DMG range average + ToHitBonus average = avg number of hits to kill
