Refinement-2 backlog (from live playtest 26-07-24 -- see REFINEMENT-2-REVIEW.md):
      monster natural-1 self-hit/lose-turn; SETTINGS "Crits & Fumbles" toggle @done(26-07-24)
      each with a CON/DEX/WIS saving throw; poison+fire DoT, frost no-move, siren +encounters @done(26-07-24)
      upright on settle). Verified via scratchpads/TEST-DICE-ROT.bas. @done(26-07-24)
      hot-seat seat, so [G] now works in multiplayer (was solo-only). SaveGame syncs the
      ACTIVE seat first (its state lives in the working globals and is only parked on a turn
      change). Player names are written with spaces encoded as CHR$(1) -- the loader splits on
      whitespace, so "Grognard the Fast" would otherwise become 3 tokens and desync the whole
      positional stream. Verified by `dungeon.run savetest`, which round-trips 4 synthetic seats
      AND loads a copy of the real save to prove the bump did not orphan it.
      remaining per-seat fields (armour, shield, bow, boots, teleport, both potions, both spell
      charges, char level + XP, and the four status timers), Load/SaveActivePlayer park and
      every hot-seat player shared one inventory, one XP total and one poison timer.
      Two real symptoms this cured:
        - a Wizard in seat 2+ NEVER got a spellbook. The 3 Fire Ball / 3 Lightning / 2 Teleport
          grant ran once on the working globals AFTER SetupPlayers, so it only ever landed on
          whoever was active at init (player 1). It is now granted per Wizard SEAT in SetupPlayers.
        - potions/XP/poison bled across seats (drink on your turn, the next player is short).
      `dungeon.run savetest` phase 0 proves the isolation by parking and restoring two seats with
      distinct kit; reverting the fix makes it fail with the exact player-visible symptoms.
      NOTE: `loiter` (lingering-danger meter) and `curio_cool` stay RUN-WIDE on purpose -- they
      read as "how restless the dungeon is", not as something a player carries.
    ☐ Tune the curio/trap/potion odds + saving-throw math against playtest feel (constants in
      assets/data/<pack>/tuning.txt now, not DUNGEON.BI).
    ☐ GOLD TARGETS ARE NOT A CONSTRAINT (measured 26-07-29 with `dungeon.run econdump`).
      The binding constraint is finding the Level Key and surviving, not gathering gold; the
      class win totals barely differentiate the classes. This PREDATES the item-odds change
      (which roughly doubled gold on levels 3-9 by substituting fewer items -- before it the
      board held ~183,000, still enough to fund a Wizard by level 3).
      Levers, all data-only, re-measure with econdump after each: raise the class targets,
      cut treasures.txt gold values, or raise ITEM_PCT so more rooms pay an item instead of
      gold. A DESIGN call -- econdump makes it a 2-second check instead of a playthrough.
      (8333 vs 9000) because slot 3 was a HUGE SAPPHIRE at 6000, below anything on levels 7-8.
      Levels 7-9 are this project's own invention (the board game has 6), so there is no
      canonical list to match: level 9 is now the deepest prize at 11000/12000/13000
      L6 7000 -> L7 8000 -> L8 9000 -> L9 12000. All three names resolve to existing sprites
      via TreasureSprite$'s keyword fallback (GEM/DIAMOND -> ruby-necklace, HOARD -> sack-of-gold).
      NOTE: this raises total board gold ~357k -> ~383k, so it makes the over-funding below
      slightly WORSE. It fixes the ordering, not the scale -- the scale is the item above.
    ☐ Board legend art: add "$ = recoverable treasure" and a "fallen-body = an adventurer died here"
      marker to the baked .ans (art-side edit; the code already draws both via DrawEntities).

